# Security Baseline

## Secrets
- Never commit `.env`, private keys, tokens, or connection strings. Use `.env.example` with placeholders.
- Do not log secrets, full auth headers, or card/PII.
- Rotate any secret that appeared in chat or a PR diff; treat chat as leaked.
- Prefer OS/secret manager / CI secrets over hardcoded defaults.

## Web / API
- CORS: allow explicit origins in production; no `*` with credentials.
- SQL: parameterized queries / JPA only — never string-concat user input into SQL/JPQL.
- XSS: do not `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` / `innerHTML` with unsanitized user content.
- CSRF: follow framework defaults for cookie-session apps; for JWT bearer APIs document the threat model.
- Authz: check resource ownership server-side; never trust client-sent `userId` alone.

## Dependencies
- Do not add packages for one-liners already in stdlib.
- Pin versions; avoid installing unknown Git URLs in production apps.

## When generating code
- Default to deny-by-default auth on new endpoints.
- Flag TODO `SECURITY:` if auth is deferred — do not silently ship open write APIs.
